Mission Local reported that the mayor’s upzoning plan would no longer apply to buildings with three or more rent-controlled apartments. The amendment was accepted by Mayor Daniel Lurie and, according to Mission Local’s analysis, exempted at least 84,000 rental units in 11,700 buildings, along with any ground-floor retail beneath them. Two-unit buildings were not covered and remained in the plan.

